sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant W as WebhookController
    participant K as Kafka (meeting.events)
    participant MC as MeetingEventConsumer
    participant MS as MeetingService
    participant TS as TranscriptService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant RK as Kafka (transcript.reconstruct)
    participant RC as TranscriptReconstructConsumer
    participant ST as StorageService

    Note over C,ST: Happy path — meeting.started → N transcripts → meeting.ended → reconstruction

    C->>W: POST /api/v1/webhooks (meeting.started)
    W->>W: verify HMAC + validate envelope
    W->>K: publish raw event (key = sessionId)
    W-->>C: 202 Accepted
    K->>MC: deliver meeting.started
    MC->>MS: handleMeetingStarted
    MS->>DB: upsert Meeting, create Session (LIVE)

    loop each transcript chunk (1..N)
        C->>W: POST /api/v1/webhooks (meeting.transcript)
        W->>K: publish raw event (key = sessionId)
        W-->>C: 202 Accepted
        K->>MC: deliver meeting.transcript
        MC->>TS: handleTranscript
        TS->>DB: dedup on transcriptId, insert segment
    end

    C->>W: POST /api/v1/webhooks (meeting.ended)
    W->>K: publish raw event (key = sessionId)
    W-->>C: 202 Accepted
    K->>MC: deliver meeting.ended
    MC->>MS: handleMeetingEnded
    MS->>DB: set Session ENDED + endedAt
    MS->>RK: publish reconstruct task (key = sessionId)
    RK->>RC: deliver reconstruct task
    RC->>DB: load segments ordered by sequenceNumber
    RC->>ST: store assembled transcript
    ST-->>RC: transcript URI
    RC->>DB: persist transcriptUri on Session

    C->>W: GET /meetings/{id}/sessions/{sessionId}/transcript
    W->>DB: load ordered segments + metadata
    W-->>C: 200 OK (ordered transcript JSON)
